# User Stories – DIY Recipe Web Application

## Overview
This document outlines the key user stories for the DIY Recipe Web Application. These stories describe the interactions users will have with the system and guide development priorities.

---

## User Stories

### US-01: User Registration
**As a new user**, I want to create an account so that I can access personalized features.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- User can enter name, email, and password
- System validates email format
- Password must meet security requirements
- User account is successfully created and stored

---

### US-02: User Login
**As a registered user**, I want to log in so that I can access my account.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- User can enter email and password
- System verifies credentials
- User is redirected to homepage/dashboard upon success
- Error message shown for invalid login

---

### US-03: User Logout
**As a logged-in user**, I want to log out so that my account remains secure.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- Logout button is visible
- Clicking logout ends session
- User is redirected to homepage/login page

---

### US-04: View Recipes
**As a user**, I want to browse DIY recipes so that I can explore available options.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- Recipes are displayed in a list/grid
- Each recipe shows title, image, and short description
- Page loads efficiently

---

### US-05: View Recipe Details
**As a user**, I want to view detailed information about a recipe so that I can follow it.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- Clicking a recipe opens detailed view
- Shows ingredients, steps, and images
- Clear and readable layout

---

### US-06: Search Recipes
**As a user**, I want to search for recipes so that I can quickly find specific ones.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- Search bar is available
- Results update based on keyword input
- Shows relevant recipes only

---

### US-07: Add Recipe
**As a logged-in user**, I want to upload my own DIY recipe so that I can share it with others.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- User can input title, ingredients, steps, and image
- Form validation is applied
- Recipe is saved and displayed publicly

---

### US-08: Edit/Delete Recipe
**As a user**, I want to edit or delete my own recipes so that I can manage my content.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- Edit/Delete options available for user's own recipes
- Changes are saved correctly
- Deletion removes recipe from system

---

### US-09: Save/Favorite Recipes
**As a user**, I want to save recipes so that I can access them later easily.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- “Save” or “Favorite” button is available
- Saved recipes are stored in user profile
- User can view saved recipes list

---

### US-10: Responsive Design
**As a user**, I want the website to work on different devices so that I can use it anywhere.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- Layout adapts to mobile, tablet, and desktop
- No broken UI elements
- Navigation remains usable

---

## Notes
- These user stories will guide the MVP development.
- Additional features may be added in later iterations.
